Karahan's presiding figure: teacher-to-room. One figure at the center, everyone else seated and facing up at it. That's the "transmit across generations" grammar — here's how you say something to people who aren't here yet.
Same grammar family, different roles. Not "one site got it right and the other got it wrong." Two communities using the same toolkit to solve two related but distinct problems: how do I talk to a peer I don't share a language with, and how do I leave a message for descendants I'll never meet.
